- # `↯/s.106.3` — `Json.Provider.Error`
+ # `↯/s.106.3` — `Json.Provider.Error`

- Raised when a JSON value does not satisfy the schema it is being
- validated against.
+ Sollevato quando un valore JSON non soddisfa lo schema rispetto a cui viene validato.

- ## Cause
+ ## Causa

- Jacinta's `Json.Provider` validates JSON values against a schema as a record's fields are read,
- and reports each mismatch via this error, through the `Tactic` of the code reading the field, so
- that a validating reader can collect them all. The message is `the
- JSON was not valid according to the schema because $reason`.
+ Il `Json.Provider` di Jacinta valida i valori JSON rispetto a uno schema man mano che i campi di un
+ record vengono letti, e segnala ogni discrepanza tramite questo errore, attraverso la `Tactic` del
+ codice che legge il campo, così che un lettore che valida possa raccoglierle tutte. Il messaggio è
+ `the JSON was not valid according to the schema because $reason`.

- ## Variants
+ ## Varianti

- ```tabular
+ ```tabular

- column  Code
- column  Reason
- column  Meaning
- column  Message
- column  Resolution
- row  `↯/s.106.3.1`  `JsonType`  The value's type does not match what the schema requires.  `[↯/s.106.3.1] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because expected JSON type number, but found string`  Provide a value of the type the schema requires, or relax the schema if the type is genuinely flexible.
- row  `↯/s.106.3.2`  `MissingValue`  A required value is absent from the JSON. The reason names the missing field where it is known.  `[↯/s.106.3.2] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the value of locality was missing`  Add the missing field, or mark it optional in the schema.
- row  `↯/s.106.3.3`  `IntOutOfRange`  An integer value falls outside the `minimum`/`maximum` allowed by the schema. Raised by the `"integer!"` provider type; an absent bound is `Unset` rather than a sentinel.  `[↯/s.106.3.3] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the value was not between 1 and 99`  Constrain the value to the schema's permitted range.
- row  `↯/s.106.3.4`  `PatternMismatch`  A string value does not match the regular expression in the schema's `pattern`.  `[↯/s.106.3.4] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the value did not conform to the regular expression [a-z]+`  Adjust the value to match the schema's pattern, or loosen the pattern.
- row  `↯/s.106.3.5`  `NumberOutOfRange`  A number falls outside the `minimum`/`maximum` (or exclusive bounds) the schema declares. Raised by the `"number!"` provider type.  `[↯/s.106.3.5] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the number was not between -90.0 and 90.0`  Constrain the value to the schema's permitted range.
- row  `↯/s.106.3.6`  `LengthOutOfRange`  A string's length falls outside the schema's `minLength`/`maxLength`. Raised by the `"string!"` provider type.  `[↯/s.106.3.6] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the string's length was not between 1 and 214`  Shorten or lengthen the value to fit the schema.
- row  `↯/s.106.3.7`  `NotPermitted`  A string is not one of the schema's `enum` values (or its `const`). Raised by the `"enum"` provider type.  `[↯/s.106.3.7] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the value Polygon was not one of Point`  Use one of the listed values, or extend the schema's `enum`.
- row  `↯/s.106.3.8`  `UnexpectedKind`  A value is of a JSON kind which none of the alternatives of its union (`anyOf`, `oneOf`, or a `type` naming several) accepts.  `[↯/s.106.3.8] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the value was a JSON boolean, which is not one of string, number`  Give a value of one of the kinds the schema lists.
- row  `↯/s.106.3.9`  `Unparsable`  A string's text is not valid for its `format`: a `json-pointer` or a `regex` which does not parse.  `[↯/s.106.3.9] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the value a[ is not a valid regex`  Correct the value so that it parses in its format.
+ column  Codice
+ column  Motivo
+ column  Significato
+ column  Messaggio
+ column  Soluzione
+ row  `↯/s.106.3.1`  `JsonType`  Il tipo del valore non corrisponde a quello richiesto dallo schema.  `[↯/s.106.3.1] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because expected JSON type number, but found string`  Fornisci un valore del tipo richiesto dallo schema, o allenta lo schema se il tipo è davvero flessibile.
+ row  `↯/s.106.3.2`  `MissingValue`  Un valore obbligatorio è assente dal JSON. Il motivo nomina il campo mancante dove è noto.  `[↯/s.106.3.2] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the value of locality was missing`  Aggiungi il campo mancante, o contrassegnalo come opzionale nello schema.
+ row  `↯/s.106.3.3`  `IntOutOfRange`  Un valore intero cade fuori dal `minimum`/`maximum` ammesso dallo schema. Sollevato dal tipo di provider `"integer!"`; un limite assente è `Unset` anziché un segnaposto.  `[↯/s.106.3.3] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the value was not between 1 and 99`  Limita il valore all'intervallo ammesso dallo schema.
+ row  `↯/s.106.3.4`  `PatternMismatch`  Un valore stringa non corrisponde all'espressione regolare nel `pattern` dello schema.  `[↯/s.106.3.4] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the value did not conform to the regular expression [a-z]+`  Adatta il valore al pattern dello schema, o allenta il pattern.
+ row  `↯/s.106.3.5`  `NumberOutOfRange`  Un numero cade fuori dal `minimum`/`maximum` (o dai limiti esclusivi) che lo schema dichiara. Sollevato dal tipo di provider `"number!"`.  `[↯/s.106.3.5] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the number was not between -90.0 and 90.0`  Limita il valore all'intervallo ammesso dallo schema.
+ row  `↯/s.106.3.6`  `LengthOutOfRange`  La lunghezza di una stringa cade fuori dal `minLength`/`maxLength` dello schema. Sollevato dal tipo di provider `"string!"`.  `[↯/s.106.3.6] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the string's length was not between 1 and 214`  Accorcia o allunga il valore perché rientri nello schema.
+ row  `↯/s.106.3.7`  `NotPermitted`  Una stringa non è uno dei valori `enum` dello schema (o il suo `const`). Sollevato dal tipo di provider `"enum"`.  `[↯/s.106.3.7] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the value Polygon was not one of Point`  Usa uno dei valori elencati, o estendi l'`enum` dello schema.
+ row  `↯/s.106.3.8`  `UnexpectedKind`  Un valore è di un genere JSON che nessuna delle alternative della sua unione (`anyOf`, `oneOf`, o un `type` che ne nomina diversi) accetta.  `[↯/s.106.3.8] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the value was a JSON boolean, which is not one of string, number`  Fornisci un valore di uno dei generi elencati dallo schema.
+ row  `↯/s.106.3.9`  `Unparsable`  Il testo di una stringa non è valido per il suo `format`: un `json-pointer` o una `regex` che non supera il parsing.  `[↯/s.106.3.9] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the value a[ is not a valid regex`  Correggi il valore perché superi il parsing nel suo formato.

